    "When a larger container type is used to satisfy the demand of a smaller type, does that larger container count as one unit of the smaller type's demand (i.e., one large container fulfills exactly one unit of the smaller demand), or is the substitution measured by volume (i.e., the number of smaller units covered equals the volume ratio)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how substitution is measured (unit count vs. volume ratio), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

